<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>

    <!--
        Special Holding / SH Reason, visible only to the Special Holding
        Authority group (COMP-2026-00052: Documentation Staff must no longer
        see or set them).

        WHY VIEW-LEVEL AND NOT FIELD-LEVEL
        ==================================
        The obvious mechanism, Field Access Groups on the field itself, is a
        SILENT NO-OP for Studio fields in Odoo 17. IrModelFields._instanciate_attrs()
        builds a manual field from field_description / help / index / copied /
        related / required / readonly / store / company_dependent; `groups` is
        not in that list, so the row lands in ir_model_fields_group_rel and the
        registry never reads it. Proven on a production restore: with the rel
        rows present and after a real service restart, a non-member could still
        read(), search(), reach the value from a server action and see it in
        fields_get(). And base (code-declared) fields cannot be given `groups`
        from the UI at all: ir.model.fields.write refuses with "Properties of
        base fields cannot be altered in this manner!".

        View-level `groups` on the field NODE is therefore the mechanism. It has
        a second property that matters here: it never touches the ORM, so no
        automation or server action can break. That was decisive: server
        actions 293 / 295 / 317 all read x_studio_special_holding as the acting
        user with no sudo(), and automations 2 / 4 / 15 fire on ordinary picking
        save and validation by Documentation Staff. A field-level restriction
        would have made those crash for Docs Staff.

        RESTRICT THE TWO FIELDS AS A PAIR, NEVER ONE ALONE
        ==================================================
        In the picking form, SH Reason carries
        readonly="not x_studio_special_holding or ...". Both nodes must drop
        together or that modifier references a field no longer in the view.

        KNOWN LIMITATION, ACCEPTED
        ==========================
        View-level is UI-only. The values stay reachable by export, RPC or a
        dev-mode custom filter to anyone who knows the technical field name.
        Closing that needs groups= on the Python fields in this module PLUS
        .sudo() on the reads in SA 293 / 295 / 317.

        stock.quant.history also exposes both fields, and is deliberately NOT
        restricted here: Documentation Staff have no ACL on that model at all,
        so the screen is already unreachable for them.
    -->

    <record id="view_stock_move_line_ops_sh_restrict" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">stock.move.line.ops.sh.restrict</field>
        <field name="model">stock.move.line</field>
        <field name="inherit_id" ref="multiple_relocation.view_stock_move_line_detailed_operation_tree_inherit"/>
        <field name="priority">200</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <xpath expr="//field[@name='x_studio_special_holding']" position="attributes">
                <attribute name="groups">multiple_relocation.group_special_holding_authority</attribute>
            </xpath>
            <xpath expr="//field[@name='x_studio_sh_reason']" position="attributes">
                <attribute name="groups">multiple_relocation.group_special_holding_authority</attribute>
            </xpath>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="view_stock_picking_form_sh_restrict" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="name">stock.picking.form.sh.restrict</field>
        <field name="model">stock.picking</field>
        <field name="inherit_id" ref="multiple_relocation.view_stock_picking_form_custom"/>
        <field name="priority">200</field>
        <field name="arch" type="xml">
            <xpath expr="//field[@name='x_studio_special_holding']" position="attributes">
